<p></p>
<p>
 <br>
</p>
<p>The compass module menu facilitates the primary navigation on each page =
of the application.&nbsp;</p>
<p>The following describes how the module menu should be behave to effectiv=
ely facilitate the navigation within the platform.&nbsp;</p>
<h2 id=3D"CompassModuleNavigation-MenuPreparation">Menu Preparation</h2>
<p>Before rendering the menu, determine which of all the nodes the user can=
 access and only show those.</p>
<ul>
 <li>Check module resource assignment
  <ul>
   <li>Each node that opens a module should have an accompanying resource t=
o control access to that module</li>
   <li>If this resource isn't available within the looked in users resource=
 assignments, then remove the node</li>
  </ul></li>
 <li>Check dependent linked account ids needed to see
  <ul>
   <li>Some nodes require a linked account to the system powering the modul=
e</li>
   <li>Examples:
    <ul>
     <li>Compass (Legacy)&nbsp;
      <ul>
       <li>Compass (Legacy) User ID</li>
      </ul></li>
     <li>Servicing, Servicing: Approvals
      <ul>
       <li>At least one SecureZone ID</li>
      </ul></li>
    </ul></li>
  </ul></li>
 <li>Parent nodes that don't have a link to an internal or external module
  <ul>
   <li>Some nodes don't have a destination, but they do have children</li>
   <li>Example:
    <ul>
     <li>Onboarding
      <ul>
       <li>Onboarding: Questionnaires</li>
       <li>Onboarding: Forms</li>
       <li>Onboarding: Paper Upload</li>
      </ul></li>
    </ul></li>
   <li>For nodes with children but no link, only show those nodes if at lea=
st 2 of the children remain present after the above 2 filters</li>
   <li>If only one child remains, make the parent node function as that chi=
ld node
    <ul>
     <li>Example 1: Internal module
      <ul>
       <li>Onboarding
        <ul>
         <li>Onboarding: Questionnaires</li>
        </ul></li>
       <li>Display
        <ul>
         <li>Onboarding
          <ul>
           <li>Onboarding should now have the properties of Onboarding: Que=
stionnaires</li>
           <li>When the user selects Onboarding, go to Onboarding: Question=
naires</li>
          </ul></li>
        </ul></li>
      </ul></li>
     <li>Example 2: External Module
      <ul>
       <li>Onboarding
        <ul>
         <li>Onboarding: Forms</li>
        </ul></li>
       <li>Display
        <ul>
         <li>Onboarding -&gt;
          <ul>
           <li>Onboarding should now have the properties of Onboarding: For=
ms</li>
           <li>Onboarding should appear as an external module</li>
           <li>When the user selects Onboarding, go to Onboarding: Question=
naires</li>
          </ul></li>
        </ul></li>
      </ul></li>
    </ul></li>
  </ul></li>
</ul>
<h2 id=3D"CompassModuleNavigation-MenuVisualDesign">Menu Visual Design</h2>
<p>Example Module Menu: Firm Module Menu</p>
<p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper"><img class=3D"confluenc=
